{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data access layer data access layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md","fileName":"Data Access Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Access Layer","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 10:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data access layer data access layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md","fileName":"Data Access Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Access Layer","heading":"Data Access Layer","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A data access layer contains the code that reads and writes durable storage while presenting an application-facing contract. It keeps controllers and domain services from embedding provider configuration, SQL, connection handling, or change-tracking details.\n\nThe layer can use Entity Framework Core, Dapper, or another mechanism according to the workload. The abstraction should not pretend those mechanisms are identical; transaction behavior, query shape, and database capabilities still influence correctness and performance.","tags":["baby"],"links":["ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Access Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey